<title>BELGIUM: EU little troubled by Lockheed/Northrop deal.</title>
<headline>EU little troubled by Lockheed/Northrop deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it saw little of concern to its competition officials in plans by U.S. aerospace giant Lockheed Martin Corp. to buy the Northrop Grumman Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not think it's a case for us at first sight,&quot; a European Commission spokesman told a news briefing.</p>
<p>&quot;The parties involved have not informed us prior to their announcement,&quot; the spokesman said in reference to Thursday's news of the $11.6 billion defence industry deal.</p>
<p>Commission officials would become involved in regulatory inquiries if the parties have EU turnovers of 250 million ecus each, in which case officials have the power to block or force changes to the deal if it threatens the creation or strengthen of dominant positions in EU markets.</p>
</text>
